From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:36:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Stats for nerds: settings, placement, thread details
 and every provider's limits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Settings: Stats for nerds moves from Chat to Appearance, with its
  master switch, a "Where stats show" checkbox menu (under each reply,
  under the composer, in thread details; each backed by its own setting,
  the last by the thread details item), the usage limits scope, and one
  "Metrics" checkbox menu for every metric by full name and short label
  (statsForNerdsHiddenMetrics), with reset buttons, one-line descriptions
  and search entries (a metric's name finds the Metrics row).
- Thread details: a "Turn performance" item (id "performance", off by
  default, offered while Stats for nerds is on) with the current or last
  turn's metrics in the same compact grid as the composer popover.
- Usage limits: every enabled provider that reports limits, the thread's
  provider first, each with its icon and its tightest window in the
  provider's accent color (the theme's primary without one). Thread
  details lists them grouped per provider.
  statsForNerdsUsageLimitsScope ("all" by default, or "current") limits
  both to the thread's provider.
  Each window is one row: label, a bar with a tick at an even pace, and
  "55% left · 1d 6h" (statsForNerdsUsageLimitsDisplay: "left" by default,
  or "used"). Spending ahead of pace tints the figure; the reading time,
  source and pace live in the tooltip, and a provider heading shows how
  old its newest reading is.
- New catalog keys in every web locale.
